== 5.8 Chapter 5 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The level of ecology that includes the non-living environment is the],
  [community],
  [population],
  [species],
  [ecosystem]
)

#mcq(2, [All the organisms of one species in one place at one time form a],
  [biome],
  [community],
  [biosphere],
  [population]
)

#mcq(3, [The place where an organism lives is its],
  [community],
  [habitat],
  [biome],
  [niche]
)

#mcq(4, [The role an organism plays in its habitat is its],
  [niche],
  [environment],
  [habitat],
  [population]
)

#mcq(5, [Which of these is an abiotic factor?],
  [Soil pH],
  [Predators],
  [Parasites],
  [Competitors]
)

#mcq(6, [Light is a limiting factor in a pond because it],
  [kills fish],
  [changes the pH],
  [causes the water to evaporate],
  [sets the depth at which plants can photosynthesise]
)

#mcq(7, [The largest population an environment can support is its],
  [growth rate],
  [mortality],
  [carrying capacity],
  [density]
)

#mcq(8, [Population density is],
  [the number of species],
  [the birth rate],
  [the number of individuals per unit area],
  [the number of individuals in a population]
)

#mcq(9, [Which process *decreases* the size of a population?],
  [Natality],
  [Immigration],
  [Birth],
  [Emigration]
)

#mcq(10, [The S-shaped growth curve of a population is called],
  [a J-curve],
  [a straight line],
  [a pyramid],
  [a sigmoid curve]
)

#mcq(11, [Two species that need exactly the same resources in the same place will],
  [become one species],
  [both increase],
  [exclude one another],
  [share them for ever]
)

#mcq(12, [A quadrat is most suitable for estimating the population of],
  [birds],
  [plants],
  [fish],
  [flying insects]
)

#mcq(13, [In capture–recapture, N is calculated as],
  [(M + C) ÷ R],
  [(M × R) ÷ C],
  [(M × C) ÷ R],
  [(M − C) ÷ R]
)

#mcq(14, [If 30 animals are marked, 50 are caught later and 10 are marked, the population is estimated at],
  [300],
  [50],
  [1500],
  [150]
)

#mcq(15, [A transect is used to],
  [measure temperature],
  [show how a community changes along a line],
  [mark animals],
  [estimate the total population]
)

#mcq(16, [The two components of an ecosystem are],
  [the community and the non-living environment],
  [producers and decomposers],
  [plants and animals],
  [predators and prey]
)

#mcq(17, [Which of these is a community?],
  [All the tilapia in a pond],
  [All the organisms in a pond],
  [One tilapia],
  [A pond and its water]
)

#mcq(18, [Decomposers are important in an ecosystem because they],
  [eat producers],
  [produce oxygen],
  [release minerals back to the soil],
  [fix nitrogen only]
)

#mcq(19, [A population growing without limits shows],
  [a sigmoid curve],
  [no change],
  [a straight line down],
  [an exponential curve]
)

#mcq(20, [Which factor would *not* limit the size of a fish population in a pond?],
  [The colour of the sky],
  [Predators],
  [Food supply],
  [Dissolved oxygen]
)

#mcq(21, [A random sample is taken to],
  [avoid bias],
  [save time only],
  [increase the estimate],
  [choose the biggest plants]
)

#mcq(22, [The number of quadrats needed for a reliable estimate is],
  [none],
  [exactly three],
  [as many as possible, at least ten],
  [one]
)

#mcq(23, [Temperature affects organisms mainly by],
  [changing the light intensity],
  [controlling the rate of enzyme activity],
  [removing minerals],
  [changing the soil pH]
)

#mcq(24, [An organism's environment includes],
  [both living and non-living factors],
  [only the non-living factors],
  [only its food],
  [only the living factors]
)

#mcq(25, [The biosphere is],
  [all the ecosystems of the Earth],
  [the non-living part of the Earth],
  [one ecosystem],
  [one biome]
)

#mcq(26, [A population crash after exceeding the carrying capacity is usually caused by],
  [starvation and disease],
  [more food],
  [lower density],
  [immigration]
)

#mcq(27, [Which is an example of a biotic factor?],
  [Soil texture],
  [Salinity],
  [Competition for mates],
  [Rainfall]
)

#mcq(28, [The capture–recapture method assumes that],
  [animals die between samples],
  [the population is growing],
  [marked animals mix with unmarked ones],
  [marks fall off]
)

#mcq(29, [Ecological pyramids with a wide base and narrow top indicate],
  [equal biomass],
  [no energy transfer],
  [energy gained at each level],
  [energy lost at each level]
)

#mcq(30, [A population's size is increased by],
  [natality and immigration],
  [emigration only],
  [mortality and emigration],
  [mortality only]
)

