  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    An ecosystem is the community plus its physical surroundings.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A population is one species; a community is all the species together.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The habitat is the address; the niche is the job.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The niche covers what it eats, where it shelters and when it breeds.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Soil pH is non-living; the others are biotic.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Below a certain depth there is too little light for photosynthesis.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The carrying capacity is the flat top of the sigmoid curve.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Density divides the population size by the area or volume it occupies.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Emigration is the departure of individuals from the population.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Slow, then fast, then slowing to the carrying capacity gives an S-shape.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Competitive exclusion follows from complete niche overlap.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Quadrats suit plants and slow-moving animals.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The number marked in the second sample is proportional to the marked fraction of the population.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    N = (30 × 50) ÷ 10 = 150.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The transect records the sequence of species across a habitat.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Biotic and abiotic parts together make the ecosystem.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A community is all the populations living together.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    They break down dead matter and return mineral salts.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Unlimited resources give exponential growth.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Only factors that affect survival or reproduction can limit a population.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Random placing removes the sampler's preference, which would bias the result.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    More throws reduce the effect of chance; ten is a minimum for school estimates.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Enzymes work faster when warm, up to the point where they denature.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Environment means everything that surrounds and affects the organism.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The biosphere is the sum of all the Earth's ecosystems.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Overcrowding spreads disease and exhausts food, so numbers fall sharply.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Competition involves other living organisms.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    If marked animals do not mix, the second sample is not representative.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Each higher level holds less because energy is lost as heat.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Births and arrivals add individuals to the population.
  ]

]

